          When running standard 32-bit floating point (<code class="font-mono text-cyan-300">float32</code>) weights, a 1-billion parameter model requires transferring 4.0 GB of data over the internal bus for every single token step. By quantizing to 16-bit floating point (<code class="font-mono text-emerald-400">float16</code>), parameter transfer drops immediately to 2.0 GB per token, doubling generation speed on consumer laptops with zero architectural alterations.
        </p>

